Wrong (B): Worms self-propagate across networks without requiring user interaction or disguising as legitimate software. The described malware required the user to download and install it voluntarily.
Wrong (C): Ransomware encrypts the victim''s files and demands payment for decryption. The described malware captures keystrokes silently rather than encrypting files or demanding ransom.
Wrong (D): A logic bomb is dormant code triggered by a specific condition such as a date or event. The malware described activated immediately upon installation and operates continuously.$EXPL$
