  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per NIST SP 800-161 (Supply Chain Risk Management) and NIST SP 800-53 SA-12, this scenario describes an APT using a supply chain vector by compromising a trusted third-party provider to access the ultimate target. APTs are characterized by sophistication, persistence, specific targeting, and multi-stage campaigns over extended timeframes.
Wrong (B): Script kiddie attacks are opportunistic and unsophisticated, exploiting widely known vulnerabilities without specific targeting. The described campaign was methodical, targeted, and sustained over months.
Wrong (C): Denial of service disrupts availability by overwhelming resources with traffic. This attack focused on stealthy data exfiltration through a compromised third party, not service disruption.
Wrong (D): Accidental data exposure results from misconfiguration or human error. This was a deliberate, targeted campaign by a sophisticated threat group with clear objectives.$EXPL$
